        },
        {
          "id": "CR 608.3",
          "title": "Rule 608.3",
          "kind": "rule",
          "text": "If the object thatâ€™s resolving is a permanent spell, its resolution may involve several steps. The instructions in rules 608.3a and b are always performed first. Then one of the steps in rule 608.3câ€“e is performed, if appropriate.",
          "url": "/api/rules/608.3"
        },
        {
          "id": "CR 117.7",
          "title": "Rule 117.7",
          "kind": "rule",
          "text": "If a player with priority casts a spell or activates an activated ability while another spell or ability is already on the stack, the new spell or ability has been cast or activated â€œin response toâ€ the earlier spell or ability. The new spell or ability will resolve first. See rule 608, â€œResolving Spells and Abilities.â€",
          "url": "/api/rules/117.7"
        },
        {
          "id": "CR 405.5",
          "title": "Rule 405.5",
          "kind": "rule",
          "text": "When all players pass in succession, the top (last-added) spell or ability on the stack resolves. If the stack is empty when all players pass, the current step or phase ends and the next begins.",
          "url": "/api/rules/405.5"
        },
        {
          "id": "CR 304.5",
          "title": "Rule 304.5",
          "kind": "rule",
          "text": "If text states that a player may do something â€œany time they could cast an instantâ€ or â€œonly as an instant,â€ it means only that the player must have priority. The player doesnâ€™t need to have an instant card they could cast. Effects that would preclude that player from casting an instant spell donâ€™t affect the playerâ€™s capability to perform that action (unless the action is actually casting an instant spell).",
