        },
        {
          "id": "CR 405.4",
          "title": "Rule 405.4",
          "kind": "rule",
          "text": "Each spell has all the characteristics of the card associated with it. Each activated or triggered ability thatâ€™s on the stack has the text of the ability that created it and no other characteristics. The controller of a spell is the player who cast it. The controller of an activated ability is the player who activated it. The controller of a triggered ability is the player who controlled the abilityâ€™s source when it triggered, unless itâ€™s a delayed triggered ability. To determine the controller of a delayed triggered ability, see rules 603.7dâ€“f.",
          "url": "/api/rules/405.4"
        },
        {
          "id": "CR 601.4",
          "title": "Rule 601.4",
          "kind": "rule",
          "text": "While announcing the choices of any modes, alternative costs, and/or additional costs as described in rule 601.2b, some options may be available to a player only if other choices are made that would normally be made later in that ruleâ€™s instructions. In that case, the spellâ€™s controller may consider any other choices to be made in that step. If any such choices could allow them to choose a particular mode, alternative cost, or additional cost, they may do so.\nExample: Inscription of Abundance is a modal spell with kicker and the text â€œChoose one. If this spell was kicked, choose any number instead.â€ When announcing the chosen modes for the spell, its controller may choose any number of modes, even though choosing to pay the kicker cost is normally done later in the announcement process.",
          "url": "/api/rules/601.4"
        },
        {
          "id": "CR 601.7",
          "title": "Rule 601.7",
          "kind": "rule",
          "text": "Some spells specify that one of their controllerâ€™s opponents does something the controller would normally do while itâ€™s being cast, such as choose a mode or choose targets. In these cases, the opponent does so when the spellâ€™s controller normally would do so.",
          "url": "/api/rules/601.7"
