        {
          "id": "CR 601.3b",
          "title": "Rule 601.3b",
          "kind": "rule",
          "text": "If an effect allows a player to cast a spell with certain qualities as though it had flash, that player may consider any choices to be made during that spellâ€™s proposal that may cause that spellâ€™s qualities to change. If any such choices could cause that effect to apply, that player may begin to cast that spell as though it had flash.\nExample: An effect says that you may cast Aura spells as though they had flash, and you have a creature card with bestow in your hand. Because choosing the bestow abilityâ€™s alternative cost causes that spell to become an Aura spell, you may legally begin to cast that spell as though it had flash.",
