      "answer": "Ruling: No, you do not draw a card. Defiant Strike fails to resolve entirely.\n\nWhy: When Defiant Strike tries to resolve, it checks whether its target is still legal. A creature that has been destroyed is no longer in the battlefield, so it is an illegal target [CR 608.2b]. Because Defiant Strike has only one target and that target is now illegal, the spell doesn't resolve and is put into its owner's graveyard [CR 608.2b]. Since the spell never resolves, neither the +1/+0 nor the \"Draw a card\" instruction occurs. This is confirmed by the card-specific ruling: \"If the target creature is an illegal target by the time Defiant Strike tries to resolve, the spell won't resolve. You won't draw a card.\" [C2]",
