        {
          "id": "CR 601.2",
          "title": "Rule 601.2",
          "kind": "rule",
          "text": "To cast a spell is to take it from where it is (usually the hand), put it on the stack, and pay its costs, so that it will eventually resolve and have its effect. Casting a spell includes proposal of the spell (rules 601.2aâ€“d) and determination and payment of costs (rules 601.2fâ€“h). To cast a spell, a player follows the steps listed below, in order. A player must be legally allowed to cast the spell to begin this process (see rule 601.3). If a player is unable to comply with the requirements of a step listed below while performing that step, the casting of the spell is illegal; the game returns to the moment before the casting of that spell was proposed (see rule 733, â€œHandling Illegal Actionsâ€).",
